<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    Deliberately empty — this is not a placeholder someone forgot to fill in.

    No com.apple.security.app-sandbox: Mochi launches arbitrary local tools via `Process`
    (/usr/bin/open, /usr/bin/git, the user's preferred terminal, their own `openclaw` CLI if
    installed) and reads whatever project paths an agent reports. The App Sandbox would block
    or require interactive user-granted bookmarks for nearly all of that, breaking the exact
    integration Mochi exists to provide. See Scripts/sign-app.sh and docs/releasing.md.

    No hardened-runtime exceptions: Hardened Runtime (enabled separately, via
    `codesign --options runtime` in Scripts/sign-app.sh) is sufficient on its own for Apple
    notarization here, because Mochi needs none of the things those exceptions exist for —
    no JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no disabled library validation, no debugging other
    processes.

    Kept as an empty entitlements file rather than omitted entirely so `codesign
    --entitlements` has a real, reviewed target to extend if a genuine future requirement
    ever appears, instead of one getting bolted on ad hoc.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
